Third-party code bundled with blockr.process
============================================

blockr.process itself is GPL (>= 3); see LICENSE.md.

The BPMN widget ships a pre-built JavaScript bundle so that the package
works without a node toolchain at install time. The bundle is built from
`srcjs/` (see `srcjs/package.json` for the build command) and contains
third-party code under its own, more permissive licenses:

inst/htmlwidgets/lib/bpmn/bpmn-bundle.js
inst/node/layout-cli.mjs

  bpmn-visualization 0.48.0            Apache License 2.0
    https://github.com/process-analytics/bpmn-visualization-js
    Copyright Bonitasoft S.A. and the bpmn-visualization contributors.
    Bundles mxGraph 4.2.2 (Apache License 2.0, Copyright JGraph Ltd).

  bpmn-auto-layout 1.3.0               MIT License
    https://github.com/bpmn-io/bpmn-auto-layout
    Copyright bpmn.io contributors.
    Pulls in bpmn-moddle, moddle, moddle-xml, min-dash and saxen, all MIT
    and all Copyright bpmn.io contributors.

  Further transitive dependencies of the above (fast-xml-parser,
  fast-xml-builder, es-toolkit, saxen, strnum, xml-naming, anynum,
  path-expression-matcher, @nodable/entities) are MIT.

The full license texts travel with the sources in
`srcjs/node_modules/<package>/LICENSE` after `npm install`, and are
available at the URLs above. `srcjs/node_modules/` is not part of this
repository or of the built package.

None of the bundled code is GPL, and none of it is modified: it is the
published output of the projects above, concatenated and minified by
esbuild.
